Secure the replication traffic by enabling TLS-based confidentiality, integrity, and mutual authentication between servers.
Perform the following steps to remediate this setting:
1. Specify the minimum SSL/TLS protocol version to ensure strong encryption:
ALTER SYSTEM SET sql_protocol_min_tls_version = 'TLSv1.2';
2. Enable SSL client authentication to require cryptographic verification of connecting nodes:
ALTER SYSTEM SET ssl_client_authentication = True;
3. Set the server authentication method to enforce SSL-based identity validation:
ALTER SYSTEM SET rpc_server_authentication_method = 'SSL_NO_ENCRYPT';
Note: Although setting the server authentication method to ALL (e.g., ALTER SYSTEM SET rpc_server_authentication_method = 'ALL';) permits multiple authentication mechanisms, it allows unauthenticated plaintext connections, which introduces significant security risks. This configuration is not recommended in production environments.

