Create a tablespace and specify the encryption algorithm.
Supported encryption algorithms include: aes-256, aes-128, aes-192, sm4-cbc, aes- 128-gcm, aes-192-gcm, aes-256-gcm, sm4-gcm. Use 'y' to specify the default algorithm aes-256.
CREATE TABLESPACE sectest_ts1 encryption = 'y';
When creating a new table, specify the encrypted tablespace to enable encryption. For example, create a new table t1:
CREATE TABLE t1 (id1 int, id2 int) TABLESPACE sectest_ts1;

To change the instance-level default encryption mode, use:
SET GLOBAL block_encryption_mode = 'aes-256-cbc';
Note:
• This change applies to new sessions. Existing sessions may continue to use their current session value until they reconnect or explicitly set the session variable.
• Before making this change, verify application compatibility and ensure that any required initialization vector (IV) handling is implemented correctly for CBC mode.
Example:
SET SESSION block_encryption_mode = 'aes-256-cbc';
SET @crypt_str = AES_ENCRYPT('text', @key_str, @init_vector);
SELECT AES_DECRYPT(@crypt_str, @key_str, @init_vector);

